# width: 120
# height: 40
# The theme browser previews on the WHOLE screen: moving through the
# list repaints the editor body and the chrome in the highlighted
# theme, Esc puts the one you came from back, Enter keeps the pick.
# Colours are the only proof — the screen dump carries none, so this
# asserts real cells (`expect color`).
write x.txt "hello\n"
open x.txt

# onedark at rest: the editor body and the statusline are its ground.
expect color 60 5 bg #1e222a
expect color 10 39 bg #1e222a

command theme.pick
expect screen contains "┌ Themes "
# The theme you came from is marked, whatever the cursor is painting.
expect screen contains "current"

# Narrowing the list previews the candidate: the whole frame is gruvbox.
type gruvbox
expect color 60 5 bg #282828
expect color 10 39 bg #282828

# Esc reverts — the picker is a preview, not a change.
key esc
expect screen lacks "┌ Themes "
expect color 60 5 bg #1e222a
expect color 10 39 bg #1e222a

# Enter keeps it.
command theme.pick
type gruvbox
key enter
expect color 60 5 bg #282828
expect color 10 39 bg #282828
